{"id": "EUVD-2026-103957", "enisaUuid": "0a7dbe03-6bfc-3ce4-9bca-0d0c386f87e6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: minstrel_ht: validate fixed rate index\n\nThe fixed_rate_idx debugfs file is a plain u32 attribute, so any value\ncan be written to it.  minstrel_ht_update_stats() then copies the value\ninto mi->max_tp_rate[] and mi->max_prob_rate, and\nminstrel_ht_set_rate() uses MI_RATE_GROUP()/MI_RATE_IDX() to index\nminstrel_mcs_groups[] (42 entries) and mi->groups[].rates[] (10 entries)\nwith it.\n\nWriting e.g. 65535 selects group 4095 and rate index 15, far outside\nboth arrays.  The out-of-bounds entries are dereferenced and updated as\nstruct minstrel_rate_stats (retry counts, etc.), so the invalid index\ncorrupts adjacent kernel memory.  With CONFIG_UBSAN_BOUNDS the access is\nreported as an array-index-out-of-bounds in minstrel_ht_set_rate().\n\nOnly a valid group/rate pair, or U32_MAX to disable fixed rate\nprocessing, can be used safely, so reject any other value when the\ndebugfs file is written.\n\nThe file is only reachable through a root-only debugfs mount, so this is\nnot a privilege boundary.  The out-of-bounds access is still a bug that\nmust not be reachable through a writable debugfs attribute.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:46:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:51", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eebc70f132041b35da9ec74d5d395083125289b2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f8ab6ae1fa360b0191252677f41e781dcb0ffe6e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/42aa9feb27b600809414a3c6b0c650bafba542a9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/43082d604a9937b94ceb2e484403956d0f363324", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/15fb9e3cea55fbc378261ce35a32b0f8828f0000"], "aliases": ["GHSA-h4f8-3q7w-49pw", "CVE-2026-98703"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2ebdb4b7-1054-350a-ab20-7ceccda290a6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "24f7580e852b5472b51eea322bb78454df0054b8 <43082d604a9937b94ceb2e484403956d0f363324"}, {"id": "31668e70-aca3-3970-b0bd-a8d4e0610b1b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "44c0b39c-bbdf-3e6e-be60-5aa0880fdd4f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "84012bda-6338-3965-946e-ef06f631bfa8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "846ff93a-f298-3a82-ad79-03e2db10b91b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.1"}, {"id": "85e9de18-2beb-3897-828d-00293b588847", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "8c9408ef-3915-3122-b709-9872060bb803", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "24f7580e852b5472b51eea322bb78454df0054b8 <eebc70f132041b35da9ec74d5d395083125289b2"}, {"id": "91c34b44-492e-3743-9394-45a34eebff56", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "24f7580e852b5472b51eea322bb78454df0054b8 <42aa9feb27b600809414a3c6b0c650bafba542a9"}, {"id": "c3025ce3-90e1-357f-b633-09da9147da4b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "cbcde997-05a0-30cf-8d5a-04be65f66d9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "24f7580e852b5472b51eea322bb78454df0054b8 <f8ab6ae1fa360b0191252677f41e781dcb0ffe6e"}, {"id": "dfc8fdb9-72de-3aa9-9056-73bf9ec883d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "24f7580e852b5472b51eea322bb78454df0054b8 <15fb9e3cea55fbc378261ce35a32b0f8828f0000"}, {"id": "e1de2334-2af0-37ae-bc1b-f785dfd2e702", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "be7d6cad-bafc-3eca-86ae-